Message-ID: <WYdUiXs9NXQ.EsNxh3pqxVsJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <WYdUiXs9NXQ.7qjoJJC8C0kJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <WYdUiXs9NXQ.7qjoJJC8C0kJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/WYdUiXs9NXQ/m/EsNxh3pqxVsJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

If you have X chromosome genotypes, then sex will be needed in order to make use of it.

But mqmscanall currently only works with *all* of the phenotypes; you can't yet specify particular columns.

You could run the individual phenotypes of interest separately (perhaps within a for loop).
Or you could omit the X chromosome.

karl

